// Per-term Chu Nom display order.
//
// Every other dictionary layer only ever *extends* a term's candidate list, so whichever
// rendering vnedict2.json happened to list first is the one shown as ruby. Rows here move
// the listed variants to the front of that term's merged list, in the order given;
// everything else keeps its relative order behind them. A variant the dictionaries never
// listed is inserted at the front rather than ignored, so a row can pin as well as reorder.
//
// Rows are moved whole. A dictionary row can hold several renderings as one grouped cell
// ("巴|芭|𠀧|爸"); a row here matches such a group and hoists the row, but never
// reorders the group's interior, so a reader showing only the first rendering still shows
// 巴. That is intended: this layer orders dictionary rows, it does not rewrite their text.
// To lead with a rendering trapped mid-group, add it as its own row in
// `user_nom_entries.jsonc` -- a variant no row carries is pinned to the front here.
//
// `vi` is the key (normalized the same way every term in this repository is) and rows are
// upserts: one row per term. Usually authored from the book-translator reader's
// "Set Chu Nom order" action; hand edits and these comments are preserved by that writer.
//
// Consumed by scripts/build-nom-userscript.js, scripts/build-popupdict-userscript.js,
// scripts/build-extension-vnedict-json.js and the reader's scripts/reader/nom_order.py.
[
  // ba: 𠀧 is the ordinary Nom numeral; 巴 is a phonetic borrowing that happened to be
  // listed first.
  { "vi": "ba", "nom": ["𠀧"] },
  {"vi": "Linh", "nom": ["灵"]},
  {"vi": "cần", "nom": ["𥵚"]},
  {"vi": "biển", "nom": ["㴜"]}
]
